Subject: CPMS I03B Faithful JSON Byte Ingress Semantic Refinement

@ [refinement_uuid] 3a243923-784b-4286-aa7b-f54c41c32864

& [SuppliedBytes] is the exact caller-provided byte sequence before text or JSON interpretation
& [Utf8Text] is supplied bytes after complete strict UTF-8 validation without normalization
& [JsonGrammarAcceptance] is proof of one complete value under Cantor's selected strict JSON identity profile
& [FaithfulJsonInstance] is accepted immutable bytes plus digest root kind accounts and numeric token observations
  + it is not a generic object tree semantic form or schema-valid instance

& [DecodedMemberIdentity] is the exact Unicode scalar sequence formed by JSON string decoding
  + raw spelling is provenance
  + decoded scalar sequence is duplicate identity within one object
  + schema property identity is a later reader concern

& [NumericTokenIdentity] is exact source grammar and span
  + mathematical interpretation belongs to the applicable schema or serde reader
  + ingress proves valid finite token work but does not claim representability

& [ContainerDepth] counts open array and object containers only
  + scalar root is zero
  + root container is one
& [PathDepth] counts logical member and array index segments to the subject
  + it cannot exceed container depth for a value under inspection

& [AggregateObjectMembers] counts every member across every object
& [AggregateArrayItems] counts every item across every array
& [AggregateScalarValues] counts string number true false and null values but not object member names
& [RootKind] is null boolean number string array or object

& [AtomicFault] is the only result when a gate fails
  + invalid_utf8 concerns byte-to-text identity
  + forbidden_bom concerns profile framing
  + empty_input concerns absence of a value
  + malformed_json concerns lexical or structural grammar
  + trailing_data concerns a second or non-whitespace suffix after one value
  + duplicate_key concerns object-local decoded identity collision
  + limit_exceeded concerns a named finite contract maximum
  + internal_fault concerns checked arithmetic or impossible scanner state

& [FaultPath] is structured segments plus derived RFC 6901 rendering
  + structured segments are authoritative
  + rendering escapes tilde as ~0 and solidus as ~1
  + no Unicode normalization or display abbreviation changes segment identity

& [Scanner] is an iterative deterministic recognizer
  + it is not a general JSON transformation library
  + it uses explicit frames rather than native recursion
  + it never executes schema serde semantic authority provider or effect behavior

& [GateAuthority] is ordered
  + passing UTF-8 does not imply JSON
  + passing JSON does not imply unique members until duplicate checks close
  + faithful ingress does not imply schema serde semantic or authority acceptance

& [RefinedDisposition] is exact_byte_identity_and_atomic_gate_contract
